From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Compagnucci <angelo.compagnucci@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:05:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pack: fix the parsing of the loader names

The loader names are stored at the index given by their LOADER<n>
key, which overflows the loader array when the keys are numbered from
1, as in the boot merger configuration files from rkbin, e.g.:

  LOADER1=FlashData
  LOADER2=FlashBoot

Store the loader names in the order they appear instead.

Upstream: https://github.com/rockchip-linux/rkdeveloptool/pull/135
Signed-off-by: Angelo Compagnucci <angelo.compagnucci@gmail.com>
---
 main.cpp | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/main.cpp b/main.cpp
index 641d770..ebf07f1 100644
--- a/main.cpp
+++ b/main.cpp
@@ -1147,9 +1147,8 @@ static bool parseLoader(FILE* file) {
 		if (fscanf(file, OPT_LOADER_NAME "%d=%s", &index, buf)
 				!= 2)
 			return false;
-		strcpy(gOpts.loader[index].name, buf);
-		printf("name%d: %s\n", index, gOpts.loader[index].name);
-		index++;
+		strcpy(gOpts.loader[i].name, buf);
+		printf("name%d: %s\n", index, gOpts.loader[i].name);
 	}
 	for (i=0; i<gOpts.loaderNum; i++) {
 		if (SCANF_EAT(file) != 0) {
-- 
2.34.1

